{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"wormlike-buried-grunion","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe typed reconciler payload work (earthborn-statuelike-boutu) introduces a named direction/action payload union and threads it through the planner, coordinator, and adapter-projection seam. The modules that build and project those payloads are already within a handful of lines of the hard 800-LOC module-size cap (`.github/module-size-limit.txt` = 800), so that expand would breach the CI module-size gate on first edit:\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py` = 798 (43 payload/mutation references)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` = 793\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py` = 793\n\nCreate headroom FIRST as a behavior-preserving extraction along existing call-graph seams, so the typed cutover lands without fighting the module-size gate. This story adds no typed-payload logic; it only relocates existing clusters.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtract cohesive, already-clustered helpers into sibling modules per the AGENTS.md module-size policy (existing call-graph seams only; target 200-500 LOC; never create a module < 100 LOC; never split mechanically to hit a number):\n\n- `run_differs.py`: move the self-contained outbound sub-pass (`_run_differs_outbound` plus its alert emitters `_emit_outbound_field_alerts` / `_emit_recovery_failure_alerts`) into a sibling module.\n- `outbound_differ.py`: move the memoized effective-mapping resolvers (`_memoize_effective`, `_effective_status_map_for`, `_effective_type_map_for`, `_effective_priority_map_for`, `_effective_create_defaults_for`, `_effective_link_map_for`, `_effective_excluded_sync_types_for`) into a sibling module.\n- `applier.py`: move the batch-execution cluster (`_apply_batch`, `_apply_one`, `_print_batch_recon`) or the cross-project/drift cluster (`HeadDriftError`, `CrossProjectTargetError`, `_cross_project_targets`, `_recheck_drift`) into a sibling module.\n\nPublic entry points and import paths keep working; only internal call sites move.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` — extract the named clusters into new sibling modules and update imports only.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — import-path updates only; no assertion changes.\n\n## Testing\n\nExisting reconciler unit/integration suites pass unchanged (behavior-preserving). Module-size gate and per-function complexity ratchet pass. Lint and typecheck pass. No new CI-provider, network, Docker, or Jira dependency is introduced (portable default suite).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `run_differs.py`, `outbound_differ.py`, and `applier.py` are each comfortably below 800 LOC (target <= 700) with room for the typed union, achieved only by extracting existing call-graph clusters into sibling modules.\n- [ ] No newly created module is below 100 LOC, and no extraction is mechanical: each sibling is a cluster whose members already called one another.\n- [ ] Behavior is unchanged: existing reconciler test suites pass with no edits beyond import paths.\n- [ ] Module-size gate, per-function complexity ratchet, lint, and typecheck all pass.\n- [ ] No production write-route change and no typed-payload/union logic is introduced here; that remains earthborn-statuelike-boutu.","id":"7153-e5ad-5e20-4ae9","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","priority":2,"tags":["reconciler","refactor","module-size"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Create reconciler payload-path module-size headroom before the typed-payload cutover"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788033535832514921,"uuid":"b09ef5b4-975a-40f0-bc78-f39662548a3c"}